.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-DEARMOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-dearmor
.Nd read the bytes an armored file holds
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis dearmor
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Op Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis dearmor
reads the ASCII armor that
.Xr noqtis-armor 1
writes, from
.Ar file
or from standard input when there is none or it is
.Ar - ,
and writes the bytes it holds.
The armor starts at the first byte, with a line
.Ql -----BEGIN label----- ,
whatever the label; its lines may end in LF or CRLF.
The text must be one whole armor: base64 in whole groups, the padding
only at the end, an END line with the label of the BEGIN line, and
nothing but space and line ends after it.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o Ar out , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar out
The output file; standard output when it is not given or is
.Ar - .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing
.Ar out .
.El
.Pp
The bytes are written as the lines are read.
When the text turns out not to be one whole armor,
.Ar out
is removed; what went to standard output before that stays there, and
the exit status says so.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the bytes were written; 2 on a usage or file error, or when
.Ar file
is not one whole armor.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ noqtis armor -l NOTE -o note.txt notes
$ noqtis dearmor -o notes.back note.txt
$ cmp notes notes.back
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-armor 1 ,
.Xr nqarmenc 3
